From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:27:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/27] v4l2: cache the NV12 plane geometry instead of
 importing every frame

VideoFrame::detileFrom() called GraphicBufferMapper::importBufferNoValidate()
and freeBuffer() on the destination C2 output block's handle on every single
decoded frame, just to read its gralloc plane strides/offsets/sizes (the
layout never actually depends on which pool buffer was handed out, only on
width/height, and it is fixed for the life of one VideoFramePool). The actual
MDP destination fd (handle->data[0]) was always read straight from the C2
block, untouched by the import/free bracket.

Live-swap on L20 (150 CodecRig-decoded 1080p AVC frames): the frames all came
out correct, but fps dropped 158 -> 71 and dmesg showed bursts of
"[MDP][ERR] translate_fd ion buf get fail fd:N -22" / "get mva fail, engine 6"
(WROT0, destination side only). mdp_ioctl_ex.c:420 shows translate_fd() always
calls dma_buf_get(meta->fd) synchronously inside the ioctl, even on the opt-in
iova-cache path (mdp_iova_cache_find() at line 430 only runs after a
successful dma_buf_get, keyed by the resolved struct dma_buf*, so this is not
a stale-cache read of a recycled fd number; -22 means the kernel really did
not see a dma_buf at that fd at that moment). The only per-frame operation
touching the destination fd's neighbourhood anywhere in this pipeline is this
import/freeBuffer bracket; the source fds are the VCU driver's own long-lived
tiled buffers and are never imported/freed. Replay() (0008) was already shown
(note-vhxpf8xausdx, O80 task i-lsdqjizvl7cb) to substitute the current frame's
real fd on every call, not a frozen record-time one, so that is not it either.

I cannot fully prove on this device-free pass whether the vendor Mapper HAL
is violating the documented import/freeBuffer contract (freeBuffer must only
release the imported clone's own resources, never the caller's original
handle) or whether some other fd-table side effect of doing this dance every
single frame is at fault; both would produce exactly this symptom, and ruling
between them needs an on-device fd trace (tools/rigs/mdp-fd-correlate.sh,
logs/v4l2-dec-0927/mdp/mdp-fd-trace.diff). Either way the fix is the same:
stop doing it every frame. Plane geometry for a given (width, height) is
queried once via the existing import/getPlaneLayouts/freeBuffer bracket and
cached (4-slot table, guarded by a mutex since more than one component
instance can decode concurrently); every later frame at that resolution reads
the cached strides/offsets/sizes and never touches GraphicBufferMapper at all,
so the destination block's own fd sees this bracket at most once per
resolution instead of once per frame. This also removes 2 HAL round trips per
frame from the hot path.

Not device-verified this session (device off the cable). Test plan: CodecRig
decode 3 codecs plus a 64x64->1080p resolution change, dmesg must show at
most one translate_fd burst right after each resolution change (down from
continuous), 150/150 frames, fps should recover most of the 158->71 gap.

